// Vectrex phosphor-decay chain - the phosphor engine's home platform, rebased on
// vector-monochrome.json (2026-07-07) so all three phosphor chains share one skeleton.
// Same pipeline: per-pixel phosphor pool (rgb=peak, a=age, Hill decay), flat-core analytic beam,
// overdrive hot-core/halation/starburst, analytic glow, HDR present with hue-preserving roll-off +
// saturated-colour protection. Differences from the monochrome chain are DELIBERATELY limited to:
//   - cap_ramp_only slider (line end-caps only at source-flagged RAMP termini - a Vectrex concept;
//     generic sources have no cap_flags so the monochrome chain caps unconditionally)
//   - Vectrex default values (phosphor_color [1,1,1], overload_threshold 0.3)
// No shadow mask: a monochrome vector CRT has none (the Ambient Pass carries only the non-excited
// phosphor body colour). Vectrex supplies real per-segment timestamps, so the unified Energy Model
// (energy_* sliders) derives the slow-sweep / dwelling-dot overdrive renderer-side.
